## Summary
Add a /queue (alias /q) slash command that lets users queue follow-up messages which wait until the agent has completely finished its current turn before being delivered.

## Requirements

### Command behavior
- /queue <message> or /q <message> — queues the message as a deferred follow-up
- The queued message must NOT be injected mid-turn (unlike current steering behavior). It waits until the agent goes fully idle, then drains one at a time.
- Each queued message triggers a fresh turn (not batch injection between tool calls).
- Queue drains one message per turn — agent processes the first queued message, finishes its turn, then the next queued message starts a new turn.

### Confirmation response
- When a message is queued, immediately respond to the user with a confirmation.
- Include a numbered list of the current queue state.
- Each queued message truncated to 30 words with ellipsis if longer.

Example confirmation response:
```
Queued (3):
1. Fix the auth bug in login.ml...
2. Run the test suite and report...
3. Update the docs for the new...
```

### Implementation notes
- This differs from the existing queuing mechanism (which injects between tool-call batches via inject_messages). The /queue command must set a flag (e.g. deferred_followup=true on the queued_message record) that prevents mid-turn injection.
- The existing deferred_followup field on queued_message is already present but unused for this purpose — wire it up.
- Drain logic: after agent goes idle (turn completes), check for deferred_followup messages, take the first one, start a new turn. Repeat until queue is empty.
- Admin-only command (same as /bash).
